  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday night through Wednesday)\nIssued at 1200 AM CDT Thu Sep 17 2026\n\nThe upper ridge remains in control over the weekend with \nseabreeze type convection happening across the middle Texas coast.\nHowever, there is a good signal of increased moisture for Sunday \nafternoon across the coastal plains and therefore, isolated \nshowers and storms are possible over some of these locations. \nAlso, an upper level trough axis moving across the southern plains\nSunday evening could bring isolated showers and storms across \nportions of the southern Edwards Plateau. From Monday through \nWednesday, the local area stays between an upper level low to the \nwest and another one to the right. This scenario could bring \nshowers and storms each afternoon the coastal plains and portions \nof the southern Edwards Plateau. There is a lot of uncertainty for\nnext week.",
